<title>UK: Gatwick airport re-opens, flights still disrupted.</title>
<headline>Gatwick airport re-opens, flights still disrupted.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>London's Gatwick Airport re-opened on Monday after an earlier security alert but flights of all airlines operating into and out of the airport were still disrupted, a Gatwick spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;A few flights have taken off in the last half hour. We don't expect inbound flights to start coming in until about 5 p.m. (1600 GMT),&quot; he said by telephone.</p>
<p>&quot;All airlines have been affected. Everyone has had some sort of disruption as a result of this,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>British Airways Plc said it would not resume flights out of the airport until 1600 GMT. All the airline's flights due to leave before then were cancelled.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4086</p>
